## Overview

- `TxDeviceMockup` observes border-box stage dimensions via `ResizeObserver` and scales its logical viewport cleanly according to `fit` without transition lag on resize, disconnecting observers and timers on unmount.
- 3D perspective modes render a physical multi-layer Z-extruded chassis with a decoupled grounded floor shadow instead of rotating a flat drop-shadow behind translucent bezels.
- Changing `device`, `orientation`, `scene`, `frameStyle`, `finish`, or `framing` triggers a brief spring morph (with a tactile rotation settle on orientation flips); `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` disables all transitions and interactive tilt.
- The core runtime never statically imports the full preset catalog, curated scenes, or export module: preset objects render synchronously with zero extra weight, and unregistered string IDs lazy-load only their matching family chunk.
- The root exposes `role="figure"` with accessible labels from `alt`, `title`, and `labels`, and automatically flips caption/watermark ink contrast across dark and pale stage backdrops.

## Technologies

- Multi-subpath tree-shakeable architecture separating lean core rendering (`TxDeviceMockup.vue`, `layout.ts`), 75+ family-sharded device presets (`presets/{ios,android,tablet,desktop,watch,browser}`), Shots.so scene pairings (`scenes/`), and lazy SVG/Canvas export (`export/`).
- Source: `packages/tuffex/packages/components/src/device-mockup/`.

